From 08416b30a3ec08e4c29115ad7a416d40b2cb94aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Advait Johari <zakethegr8@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:52:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(browser): choose native select options in the background

A closed <select> draws its options in a browser-owned popup, so their refs
have no layout box and browser_click refused them as stale.

browser_select {target_id, tab_id, ref, option?} takes the select's ref with
an option value or label, or an option's ref, marks the option selected and
fires input and change the way a user's choice does (Playwright's
selectOption route). It only needs DOM.resolveNode and Runtime.callFunctionOn,
so it stays inside the existing-profile CDP policy without Runtime.enable. The
events are untrusted and the result says so. Snapshot refs of a select and its
options now declare a select action, and browser_click on an option of a
closed select points to browser_select instead of calling the ref stale.
---
