+### Native selects
+
+A closed `<select>` draws its options in a browser-owned popup, so its option
+refs have no box and `browser_click` refuses them. Use `browser_select` with a
+ref whose `actions` contains `select`: the select with `option` set to a value
+or visible label, or one of its options with `option` omitted. It marks the
+option selected and fires `input` and `change`, the events a user's choice
+fires. Those events are synthetic (`isTrusted` is false), and the result says
+`route: "dom_event"`.
+
 ### Background tabs
 
 `browser_open_tab` opens a tab in the bound window without selecting it or
